 852:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_client.c ****          *
 853:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_client.c ****          * Versions of TLS before TLS 1.3 supported a "session resumption"
 854:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_client.c ****          * feature which has been merged with pre-shared keys in TLS 1.3
 855:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_client.c ****          * version. A client which has a cached session ID set by a pre-TLS 1.3
 856:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_client.c ****          * server SHOULD set this field to that value. In compatibility mode,
 857:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_client.c ****          * this field MUST be non-empty, so a client not offering a pre-TLS 1.3
 858:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_client.c ****          * session MUST generate a new 32-byte value. This value need not be
 859:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_client.c ****          * random but SHOULD be unpredictable to avoid implementations fixating
 860:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_client.c ****          * on a specific value (also known as ossification). Otherwise, it MUST
 861:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_client.c ****          * be set as a zero-length vector ( i.e., a zero-valued single byte
 862:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_client.c ****          * length field ).
 863:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_client.c ****          */
