 586:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h **** /* cipher.h exports the maximum IV, key and block length from
 587:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  * all ciphers enabled in the config, regardless of whether those
 588:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  * ciphers are actually usable in SSL/TLS. Notably, XTS is enabled
 589:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  * in the default configuration and uses 64 Byte keys, but it is
 590:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  * not used for record protection in SSL/TLS.
 591:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  *
 592:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  * In order to prevent unnecessary inflation of key structures,
 593:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  * we introduce SSL-specific variants of the max-{key,block,IV}
 594:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  * macros here which are meant to only take those ciphers into
 595:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  * account which can be negotiated in SSL/TLS.
 596:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  *
 597:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  * Since the current definitions of MBEDTLS_MAX_{KEY|BLOCK|IV}_LENGTH
 598:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  * in cipher.h are rough overapproximations of the real maxima, here
 599:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  * we content ourselves with replicating those overapproximations
 600:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  * for the maximum block and IV length, and excluding XTS from the
 601:../../bos/thirdparty/mbedtls/bos_mbedtls/ssl_misc.h ****  * computation of the maximum key length. */
